<p>Contractors and regular customers can buy on account. Give them a credit limit and payment terms (30 days is the default) under <strong>Customers</strong>. A sale that would take them past their limit needs a manager's approval.</p>

<h2>Quotes and orders</h2>
<p>Write a quote, send it as a PDF, and turn it into an order when the customer agrees. Orders can take deposits, and are rung up at the till when they're collected, with the deposit already taken off.</p>

<h2>Payments and statements</h2>
<p>Record payments against the customer's account; they settle the oldest sales first. Print or email a statement showing what's owed and how old it is, and send reminders by SMS.</p>

<h2>Deliveries</h2>
<p>Add a delivery note to a sale for goods going out on the lorry, and mark it dispatched and delivered with who received it.</p>
